ADOM is a good game, but it's not Nethack.  You'll be starting the
learning curve over almost entirely from scratch.

If I hadn't seen SLASH'EM before and someone put it in front of me,
saying it was Nethack 4.0, I'd believe him... it adds a lot of cool
things and does a lot of rebalancing as well.  It would take a just
*slightly* more bloodthirsty Devteam to make some of these cruel, yet
perfectly logical additions.  It's a more difficult game on the whole,
especially for someone used to the existing Nethack ruleset, but just
remember that SLASH'EM revels in your failure and you'll probably do
okay.

Another possibility you might want to consider is conduct games.

